WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.644
Microsoft, AWS and VMware
already ship tools that

2
00:00:03.644 --> 00:00:07.150
test most of the settings
an assessor asks about.

3
00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:11.326
The gap is turning each failed
test into owned work with a clock,

4
00:00:11.326 --> 00:00:13.575
and each closed task into a record.

5
00:00:13.575 --> 00:00:18.819
The program runs one loop everywhere:
the native tool tests, drift is detected,

6
00:00:18.819 --> 00:00:22.507
a typed task is raised against
the configuration item,

7
00:00:22.507 --> 00:00:27.587
the owning team fixes it natively, and
the task closes on a re-test, not a click.

8
00:00:27.587 --> 00:00:31.824
The service management platform reads
control state; it never writes it.

9
00:00:31.824 --> 00:00:33.513
The government clouds differ.

10
00:00:33.513 --> 00:00:38.388
Defender for Cloud's ServiceNow integration
isn't available in Azure Government.

11
00:00:38.388 --> 00:00:44.033
Compliance Manager's continuous
assessments are still rolling out in GCC.

12
00:00:44.033 --> 00:00:48.039
AWS Audit Manager closed to
new customers on April 30,

13
00:00:48.039 --> 00:00:50.588
2026, and has no GovCloud endpoint.

14
00:00:50.588 --> 00:00:54.900
AWS's ServiceNow connector
loses support on March 31,

15
00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:59.312
2027, and Security Hub keeps
findings only ninety days.

16
00:00:59.312 --> 00:01:03.693
In VMware Cloud Foundation 9.1,
the compliance benchmarks were

17
00:01:03.693 --> 00:01:08.074
replaced by a posture tool that
lists no NIST or DISA benchmark.

18
00:01:08.074 --> 00:01:12.860
On premises, the agency produces
every piece of evidence itself.
